# Session split (git)

Two branches share one baseline commit. Do not mix work.

## `feat/loop` (this function session)

May edit:

- `server/**`
- `client/apps/*/src/stores/**`
- `client/packages/sdk/**`
- `client/packages/api/**` if present
- Vue/TS that fetch, map, or persist data
- i18n keys required by new logic
- SQL / mappers / controllers

Must not edit skin:

- `client/packages/ui/src/tokens.css`
- `client/packages/preferences/src/theme.css`
- `client/apps/*/src/styles/**`
- `client/apps/mobile/src/pages/index/original-prototype.css`
- layout-only class/token rewrites in plaza or admin chrome

Focus: login → plaza with real trips/demands → demand/quote/PK → unique unpaid order → proofs → matching admin queues.

## `ui/skin` (other session)

May edit CSS, tokens, spacing, typography, layout class names, and presentational markup that does not change request/state.

Must not edit stores, SDK, Spring controllers/mappers, or business conditionals.

## Shared files (stop and coordinate)

Do not both rewrite: `App.vue`, plaza `pages/index/index.vue`, admin `ConsoleView.vue`, `tabs.ts`, router. If a change needs both logic and layout, finish one branch, merge, then the other.

## Merge

Commit on your branch. The other session `git checkout` their branch and `git merge` only after a pull of the latest other branch, or merge both into `main`.
